00:37:38.960 --> 00:37:51.020
And I have very clear memory noting a time mark

00:37:51.020 --> 00:37:55.230
where the first officer is quoted as saying,

00:37:55.230 --> 00:37:56.750
stab, trim, cutout switches,

00:37:57.300 --> 00:37:59.960
which takes the weapon away from MCAS, which is...

00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:01.400
what Boeing told us to do.

00:38:03.000 --> 00:38:09.230
And I have to confess, I probably swore.

00:38:09.330 --> 00:38:10.410
I said, the kid got it right.

00:38:11.520 --> 00:38:12.900
That kid got it right.

00:38:13.180 --> 00:38:17.730
What had happened was the pilots did do

00:38:17.730 --> 00:38:19.070
what they were supposed to do.

00:38:19.920 --> 00:38:22.060
They had cut the electricity off.

00:38:22.420 --> 00:38:23.080
Don't sink.

00:38:23.420 --> 00:38:24.660
They hit these switches,

00:38:24.740 --> 00:38:26.780
and they tried to take manual control.

00:38:27.660 --> 00:38:29.920
The first officer is reaching to this.

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:34.860
large wheel on his left and that's the manual trim wheel and trying to turn it

00:38:34.860 --> 00:38:41.360
it's like lifting up a 10-ton bucket of cement out of a deep well the problem was

00:38:41.360 --> 00:38:45.800
at that point the plane was going so fast that even after they took manual

00:38:45.800 --> 00:38:54.170
control they could not physically get the plane to write itself they shouldn't

00:38:54.170 --> 00:38:59.180
have been going that fast and they're continuing to accelerate towards the

00:38:59.180 --> 00:38:59.500
ground

00:39:01.280 --> 00:39:03.200
The ground is approaching them.

00:39:03.880 --> 00:39:05.960
Then, with no apparent recourse,

00:39:06.420 --> 00:39:08.620
the pilots reached for the stabilizer switches.

00:39:09.090 --> 00:39:12.460
I'm yelling into the cockpit, don't do that.

00:39:13.840 --> 00:39:15.060
And I don't know what they're facing.

00:39:16.440 --> 00:39:18.160
MCAS was reactivated.

00:39:18.940 --> 00:39:20.840
MCAS says, hey, I'm back on.

00:39:21.130 --> 00:39:21.850
Here we go.

00:39:22.590 --> 00:39:23.110
Zzzzzz.

00:39:23.440 --> 00:39:27.200
And now the airplane is in near full nose-down trim,

00:39:27.380 --> 00:39:29.320
and you can pull back forever.

00:39:30.220 --> 00:39:35.220
And there's not enough metal in the back of the airplane to make that airplane come up to a nose up.

00:39:35.340 --> 00:39:39.950
Terrain, terrain. Pull up, pull up, pull up.

00:39:46.260 --> 00:39:47.520
She died when she was 24.

00:39:50.860 --> 00:39:54.980
It's unbearable that she's not with us.

00:39:57.320 --> 00:39:59.980
And the only thing I can do is...

00:40:02.330 --> 00:40:04.170
try to prevent this for other people.

00:40:06.740 --> 00:40:09.860
About four months after the Ethiopian Airlines crash,

00:40:10.610 --> 00:40:13.610
the family of Samyastumo was about to receive news

00:40:13.610 --> 00:40:15.090
